{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1541220-smith-kith","id":1541220,"title":"Smith Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-29T21:09:53-07:00","id":1541220,"title":"Smith Kith","content":"Again, thoughts and comments please. Ta! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2ecc71\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Smith</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2ecc71\"><i>A sword for the Spring Prince? I'll forge him one worthy of the Summer King.</i></span><br /> <br /> Smiths are those changelings taken to Arcadia to be craftsmen and builders. Often maimed or deformed during their labours, sometimes even as punishment for producing work that failed to meet exacting and ever-changing standards, they were forced to continue their craft. Some replace lost parts of themselves with tools to keep working, while others simply learn to make do with only a single arm or eye. They end their Durance in all manner of ways, often by sheer luck, or the sympathy and help of a fellow slave. Sometimes they manage to build traps and puzzles into their creations that distract their Keepers long enough to flee.<br /> <br /> <i>Beast:</i> Ant? Termite? The Court doesn't know or care. Its buildings are a cross between the Sagrada Familia and R'lyeh, but no Huntsman has ever come out of one alive.<br /> <br /> <i>Darkling:</i> He is short, bearded and grub-like, with wiry muscles and crow's feet under a leather smock.<br /> <br /> <i>Elemental:</i> They use their water-enhanced body to smooth away stone and wood into organic, almost living-looking masterpieces.<br /> <br /> <i>Fairest:</i> He's covered in studs, tattoos and grease and works with engines. He's tried everything, but he still looks like a Noldor elf.<br /> <br /> <i>Grimm:</i> Proper sword-crafter, this one. When you have a popular blacksmithing YouTube channel you've got to have the hipster beard and top knot; they make up for the burn scars.<br /> <br /> <i>Ogre:</i> She sports elephantine tusks, the calloused hands of a stonemason, and has a great round eye in the centre of her forehead.<br /> <br /> <i>Wizened:</i> She wears a mighty belt hung with tongs and tools. She has lungs like bellows, and one hand replaced with a forge hammer.<br /> <br /> <b>Kith Blessing:</b> When using Crafts to create something that requires some strength, such as blacksmithing, masonry, woodworking, etc., three successes count as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i>Magic in My Hands:</i> Once per Story, smiths may create oath-forged tokens requiring only one oath per dot. Smiths may expend a point of Glamour and roll Dexterity + Crafts + Wyrd to craft an item as an instant action instead of an extended action. She needs access to proper tools, workspace and materials as usual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","name":"Greg Davis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}